iphonebridge (0.20.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The daemon, doctor and ancs-enable find the iPhone's BlueZ object by
    its address. An iPhone BlueZ first saw over LE has an object named
    after a random address, which per-app notifications, media controls
    and the battery level never found.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:01 -0500

iphonebridge (0.20.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The daemon runs as /usr/libexec/iphonebridge/iphonebridge-daemon,
    confined by the AppArmor profile /etc/apparmor.d/iphonebridge in
    enforce mode.
  * No sudo: the daemon starts iphonebridge-cod.service, which a polkit
    rule lets a local user start, to set the adapter's class. The
    iphonebridge group and both sudoers rules are gone; an upgrade
    removes them.
  * obexd is restarted over D-Bus instead of with systemctl.
  * Cover art is copied from mpris-proxy's download when mpris-proxy
    holds the iPhone's only image channel.
  * ancs-enable names a bond without Low Energy keys as a reason BlueZ
    hides PreferredBearer.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

iphonebridge (0.19.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Clear all at the foot of the Notifications tab dismisses every
    card at once, on the phone too where it still can.
  * The dismiss button on a notification card sat under the desktop
    style's scrollbar on KDE; the scrollbar now sits beside the cards.
  * The daemon no longer stacks ANCS subscriptions on every BLE
    reconnection, which logged and showed every notification N^2
    times. On startup it compacts copies an earlier version logged.
  * A notification the phone re-sends unchanged under its uid is no
    longer shown twice.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 19:05:00 -0500

iphonebridge (0.18.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * doctor no longer reports per-app notifications available while the
    phone is connected over classic Bluetooth only. It now requires the
    ANCS characteristics to be present, as the daemon does, and names
    the state it finds.
  * Docs describe the ANCS grant as iOS now offers it: a third Bluetooth
    toggle, Share System Notifications, or on some versions a prompt.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:34:09 -0500

iphonebridge (0.18.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Messages from different shortcodes no longer share one conversation.
    A five- or six-digit sender was shorter than the floor that stops a
    name being read as a number, so every shortcode fell back to the
    same placeholder thread.

